'''Ambulacraria''' (am″bụ̄-lak-rā′ri-ä), ''n. pl.'' [NL., < ''ambulacrum'' + ''-aria''.] '''1.''' A branch or subkingdom of animals, constituted by the ''Echinodermata'' and ''Enteropneusta'', and divided into ''Radiata'' and ''Bilateralia'', the latter represented by the genus ''Balanoglossus'' alone. ''Metschnikoff.'' —'''2†.''' [''l. c.''] The coronal ambulacra of sea-urchins.

'''Ambulacrata''' (am″bụ̄-lak-rā′tä), ''n. pl.'' [NL., neut. pl. of ''ambulacratus'', < ''ambulacrum''.] A term applied by E. R. Lankester to a branch of echinoderms consisting of the ''Holothuroidea'', ''Echinoidea'', and ''Asteroidea'', or sea-cucumbers, sea-urchins, and starfishes, as collectively distinguished from the crinoids or ''Tentaculata'' (which see).

'''ambulacriform''' (am-bụ̄-lak′ri-fôrm), ''a.'' [< L. ''ambulacrum'' + ''forma'', form.] Possessing the form or appearance of an ambulacrum.

